<title>USA: N.Y. business loans off $1.003 bln in June 11 wk.</title>
<headline>N.Y. business loans off $1.003 bln in June 11 wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, fell $1.003 billion to $46,361 million in the week ended June 11, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans fell $1.003 billion to $46,621 million.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally fell $5.412 billion to $859,795 million.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
